From: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 17:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: stop counting deleted SOE states as active SAs

soe_xfrm_state_count is raised in xdo_dev_state_add() and lowered only
in xdo_dev_state_free(). Every failed or refused add, unsupported
algorithms and crypto offload requests included, returns before the
increment, and a DSA proxy state is counted and uncounted on the same
conduit. xdo_dev_state_free() however runs only once the last
reference to the xfrm state is dropped. A deleted state stays
referenced by xfrm bundles cached in sockets and flowtable entries, by
flowtable input tuples and by packets in flight, so it keeps the count
raised for an unbounded time, and airoha_soe_set_features() refuses to
change NETIF_F_HW_ESP although no SA is installed.

The count guards feature changes against SAs installed in the SOE.
Lower it when the state is deleted and keep the decrement in
xdo_dev_state_free() for a state that is freed without a delete
callback. When NETIF_F_HW_ESP is then cleared,
airoha_soe_netdev_event() calls xfrm_dev_state_flush(), which also
frees deleted but still referenced states through xdo_dev_state_free(),
so no SOE state outlives the feature.

Signed-off-by: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
@@ -3122,6 +3122,10 @@ static void airoha_soe_xfrm_state_delete
 		airoha_soe_mark_sa_dead(state->sa);
 		schedule_work(&state->flush_work);
 	}
+	if (state && state->counted) {
+		state->counted = false;
+		atomic_dec(&state->dev->soe_xfrm_state_count);
+	}
 }
 
 static void airoha_soe_xfrm_state_free(struct net_device *dev,
